# MoCoMo Mobile App Architecture

## Product split

- **Next.js (`src/`)** = web only. Do not wrap it as the app.
- **React Native Expo (`apps/mobile`)** = Android + iOS product app.
- Share API / DB / Auth / server logic only.
- **APT is permanently out of mobile scope.**
- Capacitor (`android/`, `capacitor.config.ts`) is **legacy** — see `docs/CAPACITOR_LEGACY.md`.

## Same product standard (Twitter bar)

The app and website must feel like **one product** — same brand, same core loops, same depth of care — the way the Twitter/X app mirrors twitter.com.

- **Design:** folk tokens (cream / cobalt / terracotta / gold), rounded cards, chunky borders/shadows, line icons. No one-off “ugly MVP” screens.
- **Features:** every sidebar-primary web surface needs a real native path (not a stub hub), except APT.
- **Polish:** empty states, errors, loading, headers, and icons get the same attention as the floating tab bar.
- **Parity tracker:** `docs/MOBILE_WEB_PARITY.md` — close gaps by wave; do not ship new half-finished verticals ahead of social core.

## Mobile-first

New features: design **mobile app first**, then extend to web if needed.  
This is not a website port. Do not import web UI into RN or ship core features in WebView.

## Performance over features

Gates in `docs/MOBILE_PERFORMANCE_GATES.md`. Mid-range Android **and** iPhone must pass before the next Phase. If unmet, optimize first.

## Stack

- Expo New Architecture (Fabric / TurboModules)
- FlashList for long lists; native video (ExoPlayer / AVPlayer) — no hls.js
- Kotlin/Swift TurboModules when RN cannot hit X/Instagram-class UX
- Bearer auth client in `apps/mobile/src/api` — no cookie sessions in the app
- Libraries: prefer long-term maintenance + performance; replace when better exists

## Decisions

Judge by **performance → scalability → maintainability** (millions of users), then **parity polish**.
